# Plugins

Implementations live in-repo and register by **id**. Selection/order may be injected through **static** inflow channels (config, CLI, optional args). Code is not loaded from untrusted paths.

## Kinds

| Kind | Does | Does not |
|---|---|---|
| projection | Build a read-only view from restored IR (`componentsByLogicalId`, …) | Mutate IR, persist the view, own vendor serialize |
| writer-filter | Transform validated Raw / residual toward a target payload | Skip Raw validation, talk over an event bus |
| adapter-target | Reader / Writer / Transformer / schema / target docs | Import into `ir/` |

Core `ir/` stays the SSOT (Single Source Of Truth) as an array of components. Projection output is for templates, `arcane:summon`, and optional lookup inside writer-filters.

## Injection

- Registry: `id` → implementation (compile-time)
- Inflow: list of ids (and order) from `application.yml`, CLI, or optional call arguments. Do not freeze the product to one channel; add a channel only when a caller needs it
- Public API applies the list internally (`applyProjections(snapshot, ids?)`). Callers do not resolve-then-apply as two required steps
- Defaults must work with no override. CLI / args are overrides (see `.cursor/rules/13-api-encapsulation.mdc`)
- Injection is **which registered plugins run**, not loading arbitrary user JS

## Do not

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — named in-repo projection; ids from config or CLI override
const view = applyProjections(snapshot);

// ✅ GOOD — target writer pipeline
const payload = applyWriterFilters(targetId, raw, view);

// ❌ BAD — user JS / out-of-repo module as a plugin
const mod = await import(cliPluginPath);

// ❌ BAD — write projection back into IR / snapshot
snapshot.componentsByLogicalId = view.componentsByLogicalId;
```
